DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These functions convert a floating‐point value, _f_p, into  a  string  of
       characters,  _s_t_r, with a configurable _f_o_r_m_a_t string.  At most _n charac‐
       ters are stored into _s_t_r.

       The terminating null byte (’\0’) is written if and only if _n is  suffi‐
       ciently  large,  otherwise the written string is truncated at _n charac‐
       ters.

       The ssttrrffrroommdd(), ssttrrffrroommff(), and ssttrrffrroommll() functions are equivalent to

           snprintf(str, n, format, fp);

       except for the _f_o_r_m_a_t string.

   FFoorrmmaatt ooff tthhee ffoorrmmaatt ssttrriinngg
       The _f_o_r_m_a_t string must start with the character '%'.  This is  followed
       by  an  optional  precision which starts with the period character (.),
       followed by an optional decimal integer.  If no  integer  is  specified
       after  the period character, a precision of zero is used.  Finally, the
       format string should have one of the conversion specifiers aa, AA, ee,  EE,
       ff, FF, gg, or GG.

       The  conversion  specifier  is applied based on the floating‐point type
       indicated by the function suffix.  Therefore,  unlike  ssnnpprriinnttff(),  the
       format   string  does  not  have  a  length  modifier  character.   See
       ssnnpprriinnttff(3) for a detailed description of these conversion specifiers.

       The implementation conforms to the C99 standard on  conversion  of  NaN
       and infinity values:

              If _f_p is a NaN, +NaN, or -NaN, and ff (or aa, ee, gg) is the conver‐
              sion  specifier,  the  conversion is to "nan", "nan", or "-nan",
              respectively.  If FF (or AA, EE, GG) is  the  conversion  specifier,
              the conversion is to "NAN" or "-NAN".

              Likewise if _f_p is infinity, it is converted to [-]inf or [-]INF.

       A malformed _f_o_r_m_a_t string results in undefined behavior.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
